  "prompt": "Find the common rule that maps an input grid to an output grid, given the examples below. Generate a python script that takes a grid as input and transforms it according to the this rule. Anticipate that this program will be applied to several grids, not only the shown test grid.\n\nYour script must define exactly one callable entrypoint:\ndef solve(grid):\nwhere `grid` is passed as a list of lists of integers (list[list[int]]) and the function returns the transformed grid in the same format.\n\nExample 1:\n\nInput:\n4 4 2 4 4 4 5 4 4 4 3 4 4\n4 4 2 2 4 4 5 3 4 3 4 4 4\n4 2 4 2 2 4 5 3 4 3 4 4 4\n4 4 4 4 4 4 5 4 4 3 4 3 3\n2 2 4 2 4 4 5 3 4 4 4 4 3\n4 4 4 4 2 2 5 3 3 3 4 4 3\nOutput:\n0 0 2 3 0 0\n3 0 0 2 0 0\n3 2 3 2 2 0\n0 0 3 0 3 3\n0 2 0 2 0 3\n3 3 3 0 2 0\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput:\n8 8 8 8 7 8 8\n8 8 7 8 8 8 8\n8 7 8 7 8 7 8\n7 7 8 8 8 7 8\n8 8 8 7 8 8 8\n8 7 8 8 7 8 7\n8 7 7 7 8 8 8\n5 5 5 5 5 5 5\n8 8 6 8 8 8 6\n8 6 6 6 8 8 8\n8 6 6 8 6 6 8\n6 6 8 6 8 6 8\n8 8 6 8 8 8 6\n8 6 6 6 6 8 8\n8 8 6 8 8 8 8\nOutput:\n0 0 6 0 7 0 6\n0 6 0 6 0 0 0\n0 0 6 7 6 0 0\n0 0 0 6 0 0 0\n0 0 6 7 0 0 6\n0 0 6 6 0 0 7\n0 7 0 7 0 0 0\n\nBelow is a test input grid.\n\nInput:\n1 1 1 4 4 5 1 1 1 9 1\n4 4 1 1 4 5 9 9 1 9 9\n1 1 4 1 1 5 1 1 1 1 1\n1 4 4 4 1 5 9 1 9 9 1\n4 1 4 1 1 5 1 1 1 9 1\n4 4 4 1 1 5 1 9 1 1 1\n1 1 1 4 1 5 1 9 9 9 1\n1 4 1 1 4 5 1 9 1 9 1\n1 4 4 1 1 5 1 9 1 1 1\n\nYour final answer should just be the python script itself, no other text or markdown.",
  "raw_response": "def solve(grid):\n    h = len(grid)\n    w = len(grid[0])\n\n    def most_common_value(part):\n        counts = {}\n        for row in part:\n            for v in row:\n                counts[v] = counts.get(v, 0) + 1\n        return max(counts, key=counts.get)\n\n    def overlay_parts(part_a, part_b):\n        ha, wa = len(part_a), len(part_a[0])\n        hb, wb = len(part_b), len(part_b[0])\n        if ha != hb or wa != wb:\n            raise ValueError(\"Parts must have same shape\")\n        bg_a = most_common_value(part_a)\n        bg_b = most_common_value(part_b)\n        out = []\n        for i in range(ha):\n            row = []\n            for j in range(wa):\n                va = part_a[i][j]\n                vb = part_b[i][j]\n                if va != bg_a:\n                    row.append(va)\n                elif vb != bg_b:\n                    row.append(vb)\n                else:\n                    row.append(0)\n            out.append(row)\n        return out\n\n    # Look for a uniform separator row\n    for r in range(h):\n        if all(grid[r][c] == grid[r][0] for c in range(w)):\n            top = grid[:r]\n            bottom = grid[r+1:]\n            if top and bottom and len(top) == len(bottom) and len(top[0]) == len(bottom[0]):\n                return overlay_parts(top, bottom)\n\n    # Look for a uniform separator column\n    for c in range(w):\n        colval = grid[0][c]\n        if all(grid[r][c] == colval for r in range(h)):\n            left = [row[:c] for row in grid]\n            right = [row[c+1:] for row in grid]\n            if left and right and len(left) == len(right) and len(left[0]) == len(right[0]):\n                return overlay_parts(left, right)\n\n    raise ValueError(\"No valid separator found\")",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    h = len(grid)\n    w = len(grid[0])\n\n    def most_common_value(part):\n        counts = {}\n        for row in part:\n            for v in row:\n                counts[v] = counts.get(v, 0) + 1\n        return max(counts, key=counts.get)\n\n    def overlay_parts(part_a, part_b):\n        ha, wa = len(part_a), len(part_a[0])\n        hb, wb = len(part_b), len(part_b[0])\n        if ha != hb or wa != wb:\n            raise ValueError(\"Parts must have same shape\")\n        bg_a = most_common_value(part_a)\n        bg_b = most_common_value(part_b)\n        out = []\n        for i in range(ha):\n            row = []\n            for j in range(wa):\n                va = part_a[i][j]\n                vb = part_b[i][j]\n                if va != bg_a:\n                    row.append(va)\n                elif vb != bg_b:\n                    row.append(vb)\n                else:\n                    row.append(0)\n            out.append(row)\n        return out\n\n    # Look for a uniform separator row\n    for r in range(h):\n        if all(grid[r][c] == grid[r][0] for c in range(w)):\n            top = grid[:r]\n            bottom = grid[r+1:]\n            if top and bottom and len(top) == len(bottom) and len(top[0]) == len(bottom[0]):\n                return overlay_parts(top, bottom)\n\n    # Look for a uniform separator column\n    for c in range(w):\n        colval = grid[0][c]\n        if all(grid[r][c] == colval for r in range(h)):\n            left = [row[:c] for row in grid]\n            right = [row[c+1:] for row in grid]\n            if left and right and len(left) == len(right) and len(left[0]) == len(right[0]):\n                return overlay_parts(left, right)\n\n    raise ValueError(\"No valid separator found\")",
